---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { measurementConfig } from '../../config/measurement.mjs';
---
<InfoLayout title="Contact the WinGo Learning Lab" description="Find the current status of the lab’s public contact channel and the information that helps us review educational questions or corrections." eyebrow="Questions make the work better" lead="A clear question or a well-spotted correction can make a learning resource more useful.">
  {measurementConfig.contactEmail ? <div class="takeaway"><p>For educational questions and corrections, <a href={`mailto:${measurementConfig.contactEmail}`} data-track-contact>email the project at {measurementConfig.contactEmail}</a>. This opens your email application; the website does not submit a message form.</p></div> : <div class="takeaway"><p><strong>Public contact channel pending.</strong> The project owner has not yet supplied a public email address or another approved destination. No message form is active on this preview.</p></div>}
  <h2>Questions and corrections</h2><p>The public contact channel is for questions about the learning material, accessibility issues, and corrections. The destination must be owner-approved before production use.</p><p>For a content correction, identify the page, statement, proposed change, and a relevant source. For a display problem, include the page, device or browser, and the steps that led to the problem.</p>
  <h2>Keep the question educational</h2><p>The lab cannot provide external game results, predictions, account assistance, or financial services. Please do not send account passwords, payment information, identification documents, or other sensitive details.</p>
  <h2>Continue exploring</h2><p>The <a href="/guides/">learning guides</a> cover the core concepts and link to mathematical references. The <a href="/about/">project background</a> explains the lab’s purpose and limitations, and the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy page</a> describes the current data practices.</p>
</InfoLayout>
